m1	560,250,1230,365	First Authentic Ecclesiastical Scale, tonic d.	The scale d e f g a b c d as note letters joined by dashes, the Fifth d to a braced beneath and the Fourth a to d braced above.
m2	570,450,1225,562	Fourth Plagal Scale, tonic g.	The scale d e f g a b c d as note letters joined by dashes, the Fourth d to g braced above and the Fifth g to d braced beneath.
m3	135,1685,1690,2452		The seven Greek octave modes numbered and named, Lydian, Phrygian, Doric, Hypolydian, Hypophrygian (Ionic), Hypodoric (Eolic or Locrian), Mixolydian, each as eight note letters with braces marking its two tetrachords.
